	(text_box "* consider SGL1-20 to replace RBS1MM40A b/c tariff\n\nAUX PCB\n~{       }\n* control switches\n	* PWR = do toggle switch\n	* FAN SPD = rotary encoder\n	* FAN SELECT = momentary switch?\n\n* indicators = probably addressable rgb to reduce qty\n	* FAULT\n	* PWR\n	* WHATEVER\n	* indicator light pipes?\n\n* I_{2}C display\n	* SDA and SCL pull-ups\n	* see if any info on SMBus signal integrity routing"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 256.54 0)
		(size 49.53 22.8789)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 232 213 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Ac437 ATI 8x8")
				(size 0.7 0.7)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10ed725d-d604-40fd-a741-87c72bbcaeb9")
	)
	(text_box "V_{CC} = 5V\nI_{OL} = 8mA\n\n8mA is the rec capacity, but\nmaybe should be limited to 5mA?\nlimit for TXU0204 drive capacity is\nlike 20 or 50mA, but maybe not OK\nfor fans\n\nR_{pullup(min)} = (V_{CC} - V_{outputlow(max)}) / I_{OL}\nR_{pullup(min)} = (5V - 3.33V) / 0.008A\n\nR_{pullup(min)} = 208.75Ω"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 425.45 260.2652 0)
		(size 45.72 29.2948)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 232 213 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "WebPlus ToshibaSat 9x14")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3857ed90-4006-4356-af2e-3ee71d4988bd")
	)
	(text_box "REMARKS\n~{       }\n* assembled PCB is about 8mm thick.  Probably same for the horizonally-mounted version.\n\n* external components not needed apparently, but probably should add electrolytic cap on input due to length of power input cable; assume someone could connect a cable with 6ft from the connector to the wall wart\n\n* on-board capacitors: 2x100uF input, 1x1000uF \"C_{bus}\" which i assume is the output because they provide no explanation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.7 41.91 0)
		(size 23.622 29.2099)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 232 213 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Ac437 ATI 8x8")
				(size 0.7 0.7)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "459e4c94-09c2-44f6-b382-6584207a115a")
	)
	(text_box "pwm frequency\n~{             }\ndetermining what speeds are needed to support driving fans with PWM\n\"acceptable range\" for the PWM signal = 21kHz - 28kHz (i think this is just arctic's quality control range)\nperiod src: https://www.firgelliauto.com/blogs/calculators/pwm-frequency-period-calculator\n25kHz (period of 40us) to 28kHz (period of 35.7us)\n40000ns to 357000ns\n\nduty cycle usually is 0 rpm for the first like 5% up to 100%; just assuming lowest is 1%\nso total period:\n25kHz (period of 40.000 us) to 28kHz (period of 35.714 us)\non time @1% duty cycle is 1/100 x period\n	--> 25kHz (0.4 us) to 28kHz (period 0.35714 us)\n	--> 400ns to 357ns?\nsrc: https://industrialmonitordirect.com/blogs/knowledgebase/calculating-maximum-pwm-frequency-for-mosfet-power-stages\nT = minimum Target pwm period\nf = frequency\nT_{PWM(min)} >= 357ns\nf_{PWM} = 28000Hz\n\nTXU0204 translating V_{CCA} = 3.3V, V_{CCB} = 5V:\nt_{D(ON)} = 33ns max\nt_{D(OFF)} = 40ns max\nt_{rise} = 9ns?\nt_{fall} = 10ns????\n\nidk if this is the right way to calculate the time spent translating even be enabling / disabling the devices for each pulse\nunrealistic (toggling OE):\nt_{sw(total)} = t_{D(ON)} + T_{D(OFF)} + t_{rise} + t_{fall}\n	--> t_{sw(total)} = 33ns + 40ns + 9ns + 10ns\n	--> t_{sw(total)} = 92ns\nto ms for period/pwm frequency calculator:\nt_{sw(total)} = 0.000092ms\n	--> 10869.565kHz or 10.87MHz\n\nrealistic (not constantly toggling OE):\nt_{sw(total)} = t_{rise} + t_{fall}\n	--> t_{sw(total)} = 9ns + 10ns\n	--> t_{sw(total)} = 19ns\nto ms for period/pwm frequency calculator:\nt_{sw(total)} = 0.000019ms\n	--> 52631.579kHz or 52.63MHz\n\ntachometer readout:\nmaximum acceptable fan noise level\nN_{max} = 37dBa\nall fans will be 60mm or larger, and sanyo denki's lineup tops out at about 6k rpm if restricted to 60mm<= 37dBa>=\ntachometer is usually 2 pulses per rotation (because usually fan is 2 poles according to microchip)\nsrc: https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-notes/calculating-the-tachometer-register-value-of-the-max6615max6616.html\n6k rpm tachometer = 12k pulses per minute\nf_{tach}Hz = 60cycles/min x 12000pulses/min\n	--> f_{tach} = 720Hz\ni've got to be doing this all wrong, surely?\n\nbit bandwidth to frequency conversion:\nsrc: https://calculator.academy/mbps-to-hz-calculator/\nassuming that it's 1 bit per channel\nB_{data} is data bandwidth in (mega) bits per second\nb_{channels} is bits transferred per cycle (number of active channels) ...in bits, believe it or not\nF_{bandwidth/channel} is frequency in Hz\n\nF_{bandwidth/channel}Hz = B_{data}Mbps / b_{channels}bits/Hz\n	--> F_{bandwidth/channel}Hz = 200Mbps / 4bits/Hz\n	--> F_{bandwidth/channel}Hz = 50MHz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 425.45 2.54 0)
		(size 113.03 138.43)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 232 213 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5f64c631-e027-44e0-8740-79b676d4cfb1")
	)
	(text_box "SPECIFICATIONS\n~{              }\nV_{SD} = -1.2V\nV_{DS} = -30V\nV_{GS} = ±25V\nR_{DS(on)(stat)} = 0.014Ω\nP_{D}  = 0.8W - 2.2W* \n\nGATE DEVICES\n~{            }\nZENER DIODE = < 25V\nMM3Z20B-AQ V_{z} = 20V\n\nRESISTOR = V_{in} - V_{zd} / I_{zd}\nR = 24V - 20V / 0.015A\nR = 266.67Ω\n\nPOWER DISSIPATION\n~{                 }\nP = I^{2}R\n\n0.8W / 0.014Ω = I^{2}\nI = sqrt(57.14A)\nI = 7.56A\n\n*2.2W double-sided"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 68.453 41.9099 0)
		(size 23.622 32.2869)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 232 213 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Ac437 ATI 8x8")
				(size 0.7 0.7)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc954eed-c152-4f73-810c-bf0e3e60dd05")
	)
